    {
      "id": "note_overview",
      "name": "Note Overview & Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2208,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "## Placetel Voice Agent × Zendesk\n\nOne webhook → **Parse Request** → **Route by Operation** → per-op native Zendesk node(s) → **Build …** → **Respond**. The Placetel AI Voice Agent calls the tool `manage_zendesk`; the **operation** field selects the path. Every response returns a **speech** string that is read back to the caller. All-native Zendesk nodes, zero HTTP.\n\n**Read:** `check_customer` · `verify_identity` · `my_tickets` · `ticket_status`\n**Write:** `create_contact` · `update_contact` · `create_ticket` · `add_note` · `escalate` · `create_callback` · `log_call`  (unknown → fallback)\n\n### Setup\n1. Open every **Zendesk** node and select your *Zendesk API* credential (not shipped).\n2. Activate the workflow. Webhook: `POST /webhook/placetel-zendesk`.\n3. In Placetel, add a custom tool that POSTs to that URL (function schema on the right).\n4. Give the caller number to the agent via the prompt variable **`%%caller_number%%`** and let it pass `phone = %%caller_number%%` — Placetel does **not** auto-inject it into the request.\n\n### Design notes\n- Router reads **operation** from body OR query — deliberately **not** `action` (function-calling drops that key).\n- Phone is normalised to **`49`+NSN** (`+49170…` / `0170…` → `49170…`); Zendesk user-search needs the country code. New contacts are stored canonically as `+49…`.\n- Never use `caller` as a field name in an expression — the n8n sandbox blocks it; the code uses `callerNumber`.\n- Tickets set priority / requester via the node's **JSON Parameters** (the only native way).\n- Every Zendesk node uses *Always Output Data* + *Continue On Fail*, so the webhook always answers with `speech`, even on 'not found'."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "note_schema",
      "name": "Note Function Schema",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1552,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 700,
        "height": 1632,
        "content": "## OpenAI function schema\n\nOne tool, `operation` enum. The caller's number comes from the call context (Placetel `%%caller_number%%`) and is passed as `phone` - the model never invents it. Keep the `customer_id` from check_customer and pass it on to link records.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"manage_zendesk\",\n  \"description\": \"Look up callers and manage Zendesk users and tickets during a phone call. Always set 'operation'. Pass the caller's number from the call context as 'phone'; never ask for or invent it.\",\n  \"parameters\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"operation\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"check_customer\", \"verify_identity\", \"my_tickets\", \"create_contact\", \"update_contact\", \"create_ticket\", \"ticket_status\", \"add_note\", \"escalate\", \"create_callback\", \"log_call\"] },\n      \"phone\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"The caller's number from the call context (Placetel %%caller_number%%). Always pass it so the caller is identified.\" },\n      \"customer_id\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Zendesk user id from a previous check_customer, to link new tickets and target update_contact.\" },\n      \"name\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Contact name (create_contact).\" },\n      \"email\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Email address (update_contact).\" },\n      \"verify_value\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Value the caller gives to prove identity, e.g. name or email (verify_identity).\" },\n      \"subject\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Short ticket subject (create_ticket).\" },\n      \"summary\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Request details (create_ticket).\" },\n      \"ticket_id\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Ticket number (ticket_status, add_note, escalate).\" },\n      \"note\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Text to add to an existing ticket (add_note).\" },\n      \"preferred_time\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Callback time in words (create_callback).\" },\n      \"reason\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Callback reason (create_callback).\" },\n      \"priority\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\", \"normal\", \"high\", \"urgent\"], \"description\": \"Ticket priority (create_ticket, escalate).\" },\n      \"outcome\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Call result (log_call).\" },\n      \"notes\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Free-text notes (log_call).\" }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\"operation\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Voice agent prompt\n\nCaller's number: %%caller_number%%\n\nYou are the phone assistant. Use `manage_zendesk` to look up the caller and manage Zendesk tickets.\n\n- Always pass `phone` = %%caller_number%% to check_customer, verify_identity, my_tickets and update_contact. Never read the number out, ask for it, or invent one.\n- Keep the `customer_id` returned by check_customer and pass it to create_ticket and update_contact so records link to the caller.\n- At call start, silently run `check_customer`. Before reading out ticket or account details, run `verify_identity` first.\n- If the caller asks about a request but has no ticket number, use `my_tickets`.\n- Read the returned `speech` back to the caller in your own natural voice; keep it short and spoken; confirm ticket numbers.\n- On a tool error, apologise briefly and offer a callback (`create_callback`)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
